{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01Vhz85Rx7Cp21WukzC3tfuC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The `search` service is fully implemented and verified. Here's what I produced:\n\n## Summary\n\n**gRPC contract** — `proto/v1/search.proto`: `package search.v1`, `option go_package = \"...;searchv1\"`, service `SearchService` with the single `Search` RPC. `SearchRequest`/`SearchResponse` match the spec exactly, with a `SearchResult` message carrying `hotel_id, name, address, nightly_rate, total, currency`. Generated stubs live in `api/v1/`.\n\n**Service** — `internal/server/server.go`:\n- `NewServer(geo, profile, pricing)` taking the three generated client interfaces (matches the test's mock injection).\n- `Search` runs the spec pipeline: validate → `geo.Nearby` → per-hotel `profile.GetProfile` → per-room-type `pricing.Quote` → keep cheapest priceable room → rank by total ascending.\n- Skips hotels with missing profiles (NotFound) and hotels with no priceable rooms — not errors.\n- Error codes per `error_semantics`: `InvalidArgument` for bad lat/lng/radius/dates/guests (validated *before* any upstream call), `Internal` when `geo.Nearby` fails.\n\n**main.go** — gRPC on `:50051`, `/healthz`→200 on `:8080`, stdlib `log`, SIGTERM graceful shutdown, and a `//go:generate protoc ...` directive.\n\n**Build/deploy** — `Makefile` (`build`/`test`/`image`, cross-service `image` builds from repo root), multi-stage `Dockerfile` ending in distroless that COPYs only search+geo+profile+pricing and synthesizes a minimal `go.work` inline. `go.mod` has only third-party requires — no cross-service `require`/`replace` (resolved via the repo workspace).\n\n**Verification** — `go build`, `go vet`, `go generate`, and `go test` all pass; all 7 tests green.\n\nOne note: the repo-root `go.work` lists modules that don't exist yet (`booking`, `cancellation`, `inventory`, `payment`, `tests/integration` have no `go.mod`), so a bare `make build`/`make test` against the shared workspace currently fails on *those* missing siblings — a pre-existing environment condition, not the search code. I verified search with a temporary minimal workspace covering only the four real modules; it builds and tests clean. Once the other services exist, the shared workspace will resolve normally."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":624,"cache_read_input_tokens":44889,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":624},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"13e77258-462f-4fb1-b76d-dc5ee54c61b2","uuid":"b0b8e10f-60ac-43e2-a0ed-548105899382","request_id":"req_011CbpePUVpXMKhNs5jSxMjT"}
